          "id": "item_1",
          "type": "agent_message",
          "text": "- **High \u2014 Readiness can expire between admission and worker start.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/specialistLauncher.ts` (`#launch`); `packages/workflow-control/src/storage.ts` (`dispatchSchedulerContainer`).  \n  After `lifecycle.admission()`, synchronous document verification runs before Docker start. These checks can outlast the five-second readiness window and delay monitoring callbacks. The final dispatch transaction checks workflow authority, but does not recheck service readiness or topology freshness. A broker failure during verification can therefore be followed by worker dispatch.  \n  **Correction:** Add a synchronous service-admission fence at the actual dispatch boundary, after document verification. Test delayed verification with readiness expiry and broker failure; assert no Docker start.\n\n- **Medium \u2014 Invalid private configuration is reported as pending cleanup.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHost.ts` (`privateFile`, `DevelopmentHost.create`, `classifyDevelopmentError`, `developmentExitCode`).  \n  Errors such as `private_configuration_required`, `private_state_directory_required`, and `container_user_mismatch` are absent from the classification allowlist. They become `cleanup_pending`, producing exit code 4 and cleanup recovery guidance instead of invalid-configuration exit code 2.  \n  **Correction:** Map configuration-validation failures explicitly to `invalid_configuration`; add command-level assertions for permission and UID mismatches.\n\n- **Medium \u2014 Deployed-image generation qualification remains unproven in the supplied evidence.**  \n  **Evidence:** `docs/reviews/development-lifecycle-evidence/broker-image-binding.json`; `docs/reviews/local-credential-broker-qualification.md`; lifecycle addendum.  \n  The binding artifact compares four compiled files against an expected build. It does not establish equivalence to the image exercised by the earlier real generation check. The current lifecycle evidence establishes discovery and fixture-worker behavior, as correctly documented.  \n  **Missing evidence / correction:** Supply a generation transcript bound to the current deployed image, or a verifiable equivalence chain to the previously generation-qualified image.\n\nThe supplied source supports both Review12 repairs, and retained logs report the stated passing suites. The findings above prevent a \u201cno remaining actionable blockers\u201d conclusion for this bounded slice. No commands executed or state changed; this is not approval."
        }
